================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI VehicleCostPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004) exposing loading/empty/error/success plus the 503 subsystem-
unavailable variant over an injectable VehicleCostDataSource seam. The page reproduces the web
chrome (title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the four fleet stat cards (Total
rows / Total bytes / Rate / DLQ failures — server fleet-wide totals, each with its web sublabel),
and the per-vehicle GlassPanel with a window Select (1/7/30/90d) + an adaptive table — a columnar
Grid on macOS/iPad and per-vehicle cards on iPhone — covering all six web columns (with the
amber DLQ emphasis when failures>0), using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled
glass, no raw controls). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key
names (29 keys added); display formatting (fmtNumber/formatBytes/formatRelative) is ported and
unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0 macOS
+ iOS) and an executed model harness (37/37), with swiftformat/swiftlint/placeholder gates green.

